json/key-value-pair
description: Colon-separated pair of a key and a value
- >
  A **key-value pair** is a key and a value separated by a colon; the key names the value within
  its object:
- !!<format: text/x-json> |
  "age": 42
- >
  The key has a subchapter below. The value can be ANY JSON value — the grammar recurses here,
  which is what lets objects nest to any depth:
- *: 00-json_key
- *..:..:..
